  "details": "Request: add AVATARS30 or similar scripting define symbol\nVRCSDK3 Worlds will define VRC_SDK_VRCSDK3 and UDON, but the avatars SDK only defines VRC_SDK_VRCSDK3 leaving no proper way of detecting having both in a project.\nCurrently, if you are doing Avatars 3.0 related editor scripting where the aim is to support all SDK versions, this forces you to do\n#if VRC_SDK_VRCSDK3 && !UDON\nwhich doesn't work in projects using both SDKs.\nSo it would be best to have a way to detect the avatars SDK existing for better future-proofing and current weird cases since at-least here people are told you can use both in the same project:\nhttps://docs.vrchat.com/docs/choosing-your-sdk\n\"You may import both into the same project. If you are using SDK3 stations, you must import both to gain access to the Animator State Behaviors for custom station animators.\"",
